{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics","id":1512822,"title":"Storypath Ultra Basics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-25T21:57:15-07:00","id":1512822,"title":"Storypath Ultra Basics","content":"Preparing topic for May 30th premiere of new rules on <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/they-came-from-the-rpg-anthology-tabletop-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\"><b>They Came From the RPG Anthology</b></a> Kickstarter. I plan to look over major changes between original <b>Storypath</b> ( <b>SP 1.0</b> from now on ) and <b>SP Ultra</b> rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Edit 16th June 2023 </b>-<b> Storypath Ultr</b>a preview is on <b>DriveThru RPG</b>!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/431162/Storypath-Ultra-Preview-2023\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...a-Preview-2023</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-16-2023, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T01:17:06-07:00","id":1512835,"title":"","content":"Is SP 1.0 Scion, TC, DR:E or TCF?<br /> If I were you I would focus on the differences between TCFBTS, TCFBTG and SPU. Just a suggestion, otherwise you may have extra hard difficulties and complications\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T06:38:34-07:00","id":1513285,"title":"","content":"Reading <b>SP Ultra</b> rules now, quick writing on phone...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Major changes in Terminology</b></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><b>Major changes in Terminology</b></span><br /> Was<b> Scale</b> ( X Number) =&gt; Now <b>Advantage</b> ( X Number)<br /> Was <i>'You need X <b>Successes</b> to spend...' </i>=&gt; Now <i>'You need X <b>Hits</b> to spend...'</i><br /> Was <b>Condtion</b> ( X Number) =&gt; Now <b>Status </b>( X Number)\u200b</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Was <i>\u2018Effect works in <b>Field</b>\u2019</i> =&gt; Now <i>\u2018Effect works in <b>Area</b>\u2019</i><br /> <b>Stunts </b>becomes <b>Tricks\u200b</b></span><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Interesting... </b><i>'If the player succeeds and buys off any <b>Complications</b>, then that is considered an <b>extraordinary success</b>.'</i><br /> <br /> And<br /> <i>'<b>Disaster</b>; the player does not garner enough hits to overcome the difficulty, but chooses to allow any Complications to occur anyway.'</i><br /> <br /> Did not remember this limit was in SP 1.0 -<br /> <br /> <i>'If a character would have multiple appropriate types of <b>Enhancement</b> that would apply to the same action, use the highest rated <b>Enhancement</b> bonus only, unless otherwise noted.'</i><br /> <br /> If Momentum in other games works like Rewrites - we are for a treat. <i>\ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> 'Rewrites can be used in the following ways:<br /> \u2022 Add an Enhancement hit to an action on a one for one basis. Spend 1 Rewrite after the dice have been rolled, and only if the dice roll has at least one hit (as per normal for Enhancement).<br /> \u2022 Spend 2 Rewrites to change a failure into a success or a success with consequence, if a Complication is present. If you choose this use, you cannot spend more Rewrites for Enhancement for Tricks or to turn the action into an extraordinary success. Other sources of Enhancement apply normally.<br /> \u2022 Spend 1 Rewrite to describe a story element in a scene that is now a fact. For example, the player may decide the guard outside the jail cell is her character\u2019s cousin, or that the villain is her ex-partner. This is subject to Director approval.<br /> \u2022 Spend 1 Rewrite to gain a piece of evidence about an investigation.'<br /> \u200b\u200b</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-31-2023, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T22:08:19-07:00","id":1513359,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Other changes in SP Ultra</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Skills changes</span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Humanities</b> =&gt; <b>Artistry </b><br /> <br /> With <b><span style=\"color:#000009\">Presence</span></b><span style=\"color:#000009\"> can impress someone with your creative ability through performance or creating a piece of art.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">With <b><span style=\"color:#000009\">Cunning</span></b><span style=\"color:#000009\"> can recognize an obscure piece of archeology, date an artwork, or detect a forgery.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mysticism, Occult </b>=&gt; <b>Esoterica</b><br /> <br /> With <b><span style=\"color:#000009\">Intellect</span></b><span style=\"color:#000009\"> can research a strange phenomenon, look up occult lore, or delve into a conspiracy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">With <b><span style=\"color:#000009\">Cunning</span></b><span style=\"color:#000009\"> can recognize an occult symbol, discern a ritual based on its components, or recognize a specific spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">With <b><span style=\"color:#000009\">Resolve </span></b><span style=\"color:#000009\">can </span><span style=\"color:#000009\">perform an occult ritual, craft a conspiracy, or resist the effects of a spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Command</b> =&gt; <b>Leadership</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Aim</b> =&gt; <b>Ranged Combat</b></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T12:30:51-07:00","id":1513559,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><i><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">More changes\u2026</span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Defense</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A character\u2019s Defense sets the difficulty of the attacker\u2019s roll. A character\u2019s starting Defense against an incoming attack is always 1. When a character is attacked, she may take a defensive action using Stamina (no Skill is added). The difficulty of a defensive action is 0 unless otherwise noted. Each hit garnered from a defensive action can be used to purchase Defense Tricks. After she sets her Defense, the attacker rolls for their attack action.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(\u2026)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A character may want to spend her action in the round to take a full Defense. To do this, roll the character\u2019s (Defense pool \u00d7 2). Each hit increases the difficulty required to in\ufb02ict Injury, or may be split among other Defense Tricks (including any Defense Tricks granted by Tropes). This is a simple action and may not be part of a mixed action.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Universal Combat Tricks</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The following are Tricks a player may spend hits on for any type of attack action she makes.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Attention (2 hits):</b> Your blow draws the victim\u2019s attention, meaning they\u2019ll target you in the next combat round unless combat ends before then, or someone hits them with this Trick after you.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Distraction (1 hit):</b> The target suffers a +1 difficulty on all Ranged and Athletics attacks until the end of your next turn.<br /> <b>Critical (3 hits):</b> Deal an additional damage to your target.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Feint (1-3 hits):</b> For every hit spent on Feint you generate Enhancement on your or an ally\u2019s next attack against the opponent you\u2019re attacking. You must designate the ally gaining the Enhancement bonus when you purchase this Trick.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Pull Your Punch (0 hits):</b> You choose not to deal damage to the target and instead gain 1 hit to spend on another combat Trick.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Injuries</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Here is interesting. In<i><b> They Came</b></i> <b>Storypath Ultra</b> more Injuries you get, more bonus dices to Path Skills you get. Question is this will be used in <b>Scion</b> and <b>Trinity</b> also?</span>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2023, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T14:29:47-07:00","id":1513568,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Investigation Rules Primer</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Character simply get Leads if they are at correct place \u2013 and get extra leads if they have correct Skills. They can also \u2018generate\u2019 Leads with example rolls.<br /> \u2022</span>\u200b <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When you research using a library or books of any kind, roll <b>Culture + Intellect</b>.<br /> \u2022 When you consult an obscure or occult source, roll <b>Artistry or Esoterica + Cunning</b>.<br /> \u2022 When you need to solve a puzzle, translate a language, or crack a code, roll <b>Enigmas + Cunning</b>.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 When you use the scientific method to follow a lead, roll <b>Science + Intellect</b>.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 When you have a lead and need to piece together evidence to understand it better, roll <b>Enigmas + </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Intellect</b>.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 When you interrogate a suspect to learn information, roll <b>Persuasion + Cunning</b>.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Wyrd\u2019s Opinions on Investigation:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Is it me, or should <i>\u2018consult an obscure or occult source\u2019</i> be <b>Culture or Esoterica + Cunning </b>and<b> <i>\u2018</i></b><i>research using a library or books of any kind\u2019</i> be <b>Artistry + Intellect? Culture </b>is literally about contacts with people and <b>Artistry</b> is said about knowledge of arts and humanities. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83e\udd14</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Also, if<b> Command</b> is changed in to <b>Leadership</b> \u2013 should not <b>Leadership</b> be applicable to interrogate suspects? It would be much forceful approach to subject. </span>\ud83d\udc4a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2023, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T07:39:27-07:00","id":1513872,"title":"","content":"Without having read the Storypath Ultra stuff, in general Persuasion generally makes more sense in an interrogation than Leadership do to the adversarial nature of interrogating someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T18:02:50-07:00","id":1513904,"title":"","content":"<b>Leadership</b> was previous <b>Command</b> - and in one of Actual Plays <b>Command</b> was used for <b>Intimidation</b> action alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-06-2023, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T14:27:50-07:00","id":1513971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics?p=1513904#post1513904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Leadership</b> was previous <b>Command</b> - and in one of Actual Plays <b>Command</b> was used for <b>Intimidation</b> alternative</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you know, we created an all new Skill list for Storypath Ultra. While some of the Skills might be clear renames such as between Aim and Ranged Combat, others are less clear cut. So to say that Leadership is a direct one to one translation of Command or that Artistry is a direct translation of Humanities is incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T15:01:49-07:00","id":1513972,"title":"","content":"Indeed. As They Came From the RPG Anthology makes reference to both Storypath and Storypath Ultra Skills in its manuscript, it's useful to provide guidance on which Skills you'll lose or gain based on the system you use, but they're not directly reflective of each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T06:05:30-07:00","id":1515233,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to see Ultra in action this weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:30:29-07:00","id":1515303,"title":"","content":"<b>Storypath </b><b>Ultra</b> preview is on <b>DriveThru RPG</b>!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/431162/Storypath-Ultra-Preview-2023\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...a-Preview-2023</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-17-2024, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:15:44-07:00","id":1518227,"title":"","content":"Will there be a conversion guide in case I want to use the system for the trinity continuum lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T11:51:50-07:00","id":1518318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics?p=1518227#post1518227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be a conversion guide in case I want to use the system for the trinity continuum lines?</div> </div> </div> </div>They give some general conversion guidelines in the booklet, but based on things they said a few months ago they didn't plan (at that time) to do a full &quot;Gift X should now say Y&quot; or the Edge Big Hearted should now read &quot;Blah blah blah&quot; type of conversion guide.<br /> <br /> I'd say for most of the rules in Ultra they're pretty easy to port into TC without much issue (things like disasters, how momentum works, terminology changes, and tweaks to complication ratings). The intrigue and procedural (forget what Ultra calls them) rules changes aren't too dramatic, but because lots of Edges and powers interact with those systems you might need to be a bit more thoughtful about porting them into TC, my guess is a handful of Edges and powers might need tweaks if you use those rules from Ultra.<br /> <br /> Scale/Advantage is probably the area I'd be most concerned about, I like how Ultra is approaching Advantage but worry that a lot of TC books were written with a different set of assumptions around Scale. That being said, with what we've seen it would be really easy to just use Advantage as is. It might occasionally feel a little weird, but I don't think there are any big mechanical implications.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T16:18:59-07:00","id":1518332,"title":"","content":"Expanding what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4270_2.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4270\" data-vbnamecard=\"4270\">literatzi</a> wrote - most easiest change from <b>SP Ultra</b> I put already in our <b>Trinity</b> games is change of Difficulty to <b><i>Critical Hit</i></b> Staunt/Trick from targets <i>Defense+4</i> to now <i>Defense\u200b+3</i> - it's really simple, and it's already makes combats much more dynamic in my POV. ( Will see how it works in Scion when we return to play with my other team. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Other thing is that you can give Clues for Investigation simply by spending Momentum, on 1:1 basis. It's also makes game much more dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T21:36:16-07:00","id":1521727,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of story path but some of your posts are slightly alarming. Why are you guys changing terms. I get this is a new upgrade for your core system but, it feels like your engaging in corporate buzzword tomfoolery when you invent words to cover concepts that were previously covered and learned. For me at least, when this happens it not only annoys me, but actually causes a great deal of confusion, as I'm stuck translating the Old Speak terminology to the New Speak. I get you guys are excited for the product. But do you really need to change the names of everything if it does the old thing, or are yall just rebranding pogs for the young kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T07:18:25-07:00","id":1521750,"title":"","content":"I think I agree. Mechanical changes seem very good, but renaming everything, especially mid line, seems like confusion that could be avoided. <br /> <br /> Makes sense to use the new terminology in games like World Beneath, or even the They Come From.... games as they are all fairly independent - but if the next Trinity line uses different words from the core book that's going to get confusing. Especially when a line like Trinity is already very large and has a big mechanical cognitive load.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T10:15:10-07:00","id":1521757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics?p=1521727#post1521727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of story path but some of your posts are slightly alarming. Why are you guys changing terms. I get this is a new upgrade for your core system but, it feels like your engaging in corporate buzzword tomfoolery when you invent words to cover concepts that were previously covered and learned. For me at least, when this happens it not only annoys me, but actually causes a great deal of confusion, as I'm stuck translating the Old Speak terminology to the New Speak. I get you guys are excited for the product. But do you really need to change the names of everything if it does the old thing, or are yall just rebranding pogs for the young kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>We wouldn't do it if we didn't think that it was clearer than not doing it. We've been working on Ultra for clarity, and ease of use that surpasses regular SP, and this is one of the places where we think that clarity is needed. I understand that it's a personal irritant for you, but please take a step back from ...just about...insulting us in your posts. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T10:19:41-07:00","id":1521759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics?p=1521750#post1521750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I agree. Mechanical changes seem very good, but renaming everything, especially mid line, seems like confusion that could be avoided.<br /> <br /> Makes sense to use the new terminology in games like World Beneath, or even the They Come From.... games as they are all fairly independent - but if the next Trinity line uses different words from the core book that's going to get confusing. Especially when a line like Trinity is already very large and has a big mechanical cognitive load.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be assuming that we're just going to drop a new system into the current TC line without any sort of concern for our existing TC community. That's just not the case. For example, please note that we gave folks &quot;translation guides&quot; in the free Ultra brochure, and two separate systems to use in the They Came From the RPG Anthology! project. Both of those are examples are us providing an easier on-ramp for players than just &quot;here's the new thing, suck it up&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T04:19:51-08:00","id":1526050,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/time-to-be-chairitable-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b>Storypath Ultra</b></i> design dairy this Friday on Podbean as <b>Onyx Pathcast</b></a><b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img width=\"900\" height=\"900\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Pathcast-Trio-Summoning.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Pathcast-Trio-Summoning.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Pathcast-Trio-Summoning.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T00:45:11-08:00","id":1526223,"title":"","content":"The main developers of #SPUltra describe why the new edition was created. They admit that the distinction between Complication and Difficulty was not clear in the current books. They admit that Advantage is a better term for the earlier Scale - And they say that they should not have inserted a table with examples of Scale, e.g. that the Empire State Building has Size Scale 5. Personally, I disagree with this, because how is the SGC supposed to assess the size or power of something when the player comes with, I don't know, a Scale 6 character? \ud83e\udd14 <br /> The new Injury system gives BONUSES to characters - it is taken from They Came From, but also from 7th Sea. What Devs sells is that the Positive Death Spiral makes players want to get hurt a little to get bonuses - but not enough to be on the brink of death. And that it fits the genres Storypath wants to emulate. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-ihk9v-1512402\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://d2bwo9zemjwxh5.cloudfront.net/image-logo/2761479/1440_Pathcast_Generic_Image_1200x628.jpg?s=a6dd122b2846ec6425a3c3bbbde5291e&amp;e=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-ihk9v-1512402\" target=\"_blank\"> Episode 287: Storypath Ultra Design Diary </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-ihk9v-1512402\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-ihk9v-1512402 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In which we talk about Storypath Ultra and its design! * Gas station meetings* Changes and updates* Scale v. Advantage* Competency and injuries* Conditions* Fantasy games* Teamwork* Ultra design* Paths Links: Abyssals on Indiegogo: https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/abyssals-sworn-to-the-grave-for-exalted-3e#/Onyx Path YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPathOnyx Path Twitch: https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpathOnyx Path Discord: https://discord.gg/5uckcBk </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T12:23:50-07:00","id":1533129,"title":"","content":"When will we be able to get our hands on a StoyPath Ultra core? I read through the translation guide and there is some good stuff there but I would like a core book that I can point my friends to and say, &quot;there it is, lets play&quot;. I am especially interested in if we will have one ready by the time Curseborne comes out as that will make pitching it to my group MUCH easier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:04:26-07:00","id":1533179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1512822-storypath-ultra-basics?p=1533129#post1533129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When will we be able to get our hands on a StoyPath Ultra core? I read through the translation guide and there is some good stuff there but I would like a core book that I can point my friends to and say, &quot;there it is, lets play&quot;. I am especially interested in if we will have one ready by the time Curseborne comes out as that will make pitching it to my group MUCH easier</div> </div> </div> </div>In the February <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-february-2024/\" target=\"_blank\">Release Roundup</a> the Storypath Ultra Core was still in first draft stage, usually they don't launch a kickstarter until they have a manuscript they can release as part of the kickstarter. No idea when it will be ready, or where the crowdfunding will fit into their schedule, but I'd keep an eye on the monthly release roundup posts to see when it moves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}